      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2012 International Society of Travel Medicine.",
        "AbstractText": "We describe a case of atypical loiasis presenting with a chronic pleuroperitoneal effusion in a 50-year-old woman from the Democratic Republic of Congo. Effusions disappeared with conventional treatment and no recurrence was detected after 4 months of follow-up. Such cases of loiasis involving visceral sites have been unusually reported in the literature."
      },
